PRODID:-//Rampwise//Event plan//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
X-WR-CALNAME:Century ride (160 km) plan
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-23-str1-strength-lower-body-@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003913Z
DTSTART:20261123T183000
DTEND:20261123T190500
SUMMARY:[RW] Strength: lower body\, heavy (squat and hinge) (35 min)
DESCRIPTION:Cyclist\, road endurance (sportive\, gran fondo\, time trial):
  more power at the same effort. Lift with 2-3 reps in reserve\, stop a se
 t if form breaks. Strength starts at least 3 hours after cardio (practice
 ).\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move 
 means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-24-bike1-ride-with-cadence-dr@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003913Z
DTSTART:20261124T063000
DTEND:20261124T071000
SUMMARY:[RW] Ride with cadence drills (40 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 6 x (0.5 min steady + 2.5 min easy)\; 8 min c
 ool-down. Six short high-cadence spins (about 100 rpm\, smooth)\, easy be
 tween. Skill\, not strength. Do not do this right before a run: high cade
 nce raises the cost of the run that follows (Walsh 2019).\n\nWeek 1 (BASE
 ). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means stop.\nrampw
 ise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-25-bike3-easy-ride@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003913Z
DTSTART:20261125T063000
DTEND:20261125T071000
SUMMARY:[RW] Easy ride (40 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 22 min easy\; 8 min cool-down. Mostly steady 
 endurance (RPE 2-3\, 56-75 % of FTP if you use power). Eat and drink on r
 ides over 90 minutes.\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that ch
 anges how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
